Tester #13 (box 49207, conv 48361): „სანტექნიკოსი მჭირდება საბურთალოზე,
აბაზანაში მილი გამდის. ჰკითხე ირაკლი ტესტაძეს და მამუკა ტესტაძეს." — nobody
was asked and the owner read „კითხვა არ გაიგზავნა". The person-before-the-verb
reading (#961, „ნინოს ჰკითხე") took „გამდის", the last word of the previous
sentence, as the person: it ends in „-ს". No contact „გამდი" exists, so the
server's own send found nobody, and the repeat-goal wall had already
refused the model's searches.

A word that ends its sentence or clause (. , ! ? ; : …) is not the verb's
person. The two named helpers are read after the verb, and the need before
it is what they are asked.

DONE WHEN: 3928 run 2 (first goal still working, „…გამდის. ჰკითხე X-ს და
Y-ს.") on 2 fresh pairs — both asked, one line per person to the owner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
